Pages = {1629-1644},
Month = {OCT 1},
Abstract = {Are campaign donors simply affluent people who happen to give to
   campaigns, or do donors and the affluent differ in their policy views?
   To investigate this, we surveyed verified 2017-2018 donors, affluent
   individuals, and the general public. Comparing copartisans shows that
   donors in both parties hold more ideologically extreme positions on
   domestic policy than either the affluent or the general public. On
   international issues, Democratic donors are more pro-internationalist
   than their affluent and general-public counterparts, while Republican
   donors resemble affluent copartisans. These patterns cannot be explained
   by demographic differences or levels of political interest. Examining
   variation across donor types, we find that some donors are more prone to
   extreme positions than others, yet donors remain distinct from the
   affluent whether they contributed out of state, donated small amounts,
   or recently supported a presidential candidate.},
